<h3 class="font-label-caps text-label-caps text-[#98f05f] uppercase tracking-widest flex items-center gap-2">
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[18px]">help</span> Frequently Asked Questions
      </h3>
<div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
<details class="glass-panel p-4 rounded group cursor-pointer">
<summary class="font-body-md text-on-surface group-hover:text-[#98f05f] transition-colors flex justify-between items-center">What is Pythagoras CIS? <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[18px] group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">expand_more</span></summary>
<div class="mt-3 text-on-surface-variant text-code-sm leading-relaxed border-t border-white/5 pt-3">
            Pythagoras CIS is a Tampermonkey userscript designed for Torn company management. It provides a cloud-backed workspace for managing the training ledger, FIFO train planner, staff and director history, daily report analytics, licensing, backups, and themed reports.
          </div>
</details>
<details class="glass-panel p-4 rounded group cursor-pointer">
<summary class="font-body-md text-on-surface group-hover:text-[#98f05f] transition-colors flex justify-between items-center">Where is my data stored? <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[18px] group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">expand_more</span></summary>
<div class="mt-3 text-on-surface-variant text-code-sm leading-relaxed border-t border-white/5 pt-3">
            Company data is stored in a PostgreSQL-backed cloud workspace keyed by company ID. Every company-owned row includes its company ID, and server-side access checks decide which Torn user can open that workspace.
          </div>
</details>
<details class="glass-panel p-4 rounded group cursor-pointer">
<summary class="font-body-md text-on-surface group-hover:text-[#98f05f] transition-colors flex justify-between items-center">How does the Train Planner work? <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[18px] group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">expand_more</span></summary>
<div class="mt-3 text-on-surface-variant text-code-sm leading-relaxed border-t border-white/5 pt-3">
            The planner follows a FIFO (First In, First Out) approach for paid training entries. Paid users are prioritised up to the configured daily cap, after which remaining capacity is allocated to sponsored rotation users.
          </div>
</details>
</div>
